  "steps": [
    "To boiling water add ½ tsp salt, pinch of sugar, ½ tbsp ginger garlic paste, 100g raw soya chunks and let it boil for 5 min. Then squeeze the water out, but keep the soya a bit moist and put it in a bowl.",
    "Now to the soya chunks add 1 tbsp of corn flour, ½ tbsp red chilli, 1 tbsp coriander powder, 1 tsp salt, ½ tbsp ghee, Mix it well, add it to a pan on medium heat and fry the chunks for 12 min, till it turns crisp and set it aside. (Or Air fry at 180°C for 18 mins)",
    "To the same pad add 1 tsp ghee + 2 tsp butter, 10 minced garlic, 1 sliced green chillie, 1 tbsp corn flour, 1 cup water, Juice of 1 lemon, Now let it thicken. Add crispy soya, mix well till it’s nicely coated and serve hot."
  ],
